(Distributed systems: events and messages) Tj
T*
(A distributed system has independent processes that communicate by messages.) Tj
T*
(An event is an action observed within one process: a computation, send or receive.) Tj
T*
(Each process has a local sequence of events. There is no shared global clock.) Tj
T*
(A message is sent at one event and received later by another process.) Tj
T*
(Example: process A sends an order to B. B receives it and records the order.) Tj
T*
(Local clocks may disagree; timestamps alone do not prove causal order.) Tj
ET
endstream
