stream
BT /F1 12 Tf 40 750 Td 20 TL
(Causal ordering: the happens-before relation) Tj
T*
(If two events occur in one process, the earlier event happens before the later one.) Tj
T*
(Sending a message happens before receiving that message.) Tj
T*
(The relation is transitive: if a precedes b and b precedes c, a precedes c.) Tj
T*
(Events are concurrent when neither event happens before the other.) Tj
T*
(Example: A sends an order, B receives it, then B sends a confirmation to A.) Tj
T*
(The send precedes the receipt, which precedes the confirmation.) Tj
T*
(Independent local computations in A and C may be concurrent.) Tj
T*
(Causality gives a partial order; it does not impose a total order on all events.) Tj
ET
endstream
